\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sl420\sa200\ql\qnatural
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\fs28 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Please describe your style of work and how you collaborate with others. Give us a practical example from one of your projects. (max. 1000 characters)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl380\ql\qnatural

\f2\b\fs26 \cf0 My primary goal as a filmmaker is to use cinema as an "empathy machine" (Roger Ebert's term), connecting the audience subjectively to the hearts and minds of vivid, well realized characters. I frequently do this within the dark comedy and thriller genres, using them as a 'cry for help'; an examination of realistic characters trapped in surrealistic and/or extreme situations that society would often prefer not to talk about out loud about. Personal stories, told within viscerally satisfying genre frameworks. \
\
I work very collaboratively with cast and crew, surrounding myself with a team that overall shares the same taste, yet still challenges me on many occasions. For example, my lead actress Justine Warrington was so strong in her casting sessions for my short film Glimpse that I rewrote the script around the character she portrayed. She included all the layers implied in my previous draft, and then some, so the script had to rise to the level of her more multi-dimensional performance. \
\

\f1\b0\fs28 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sl420\sa200\ql\qnatural
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}What is the most challenging moment during a production for you, and why? (max. 500 characters)\
\pard\tx560\pardeftab720\sl420\sa200\ql\qnatural
\cf0 Pre-production is the most challenging, making sure the screenplay is in the best shape it can possibly be. It is the hardest job to multitask, and requires the most amount of solitary focus. I find when writing scripts, reading scripts, and/or giving story editing notes that going somewhere out of town without Internet connection gives me the highest potential for productivity and creative inspiration. \
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sl420\sa200\ql\qnatural
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Please name three artists (at least one from your own country) whose work has influenced you. What would you like to ask each of them?\
\pard\tx560\pardeftab720\sl420\sa200\ql\qnatural
\cf0 Denis Villeneuve\
How do you work collaboratively with your actors to achieve the startling emotional layers and vulnerabilities that talent such as Amy Adams in Arrival display? \
David Cronenberg\
What is your process for transcending the genres you work in, and finding the right metaphors and allusions? For example, The Fly's incredible ability to blend a terminal illness metaphor with the body horror and monster movie genres. \
Martin Scorsese \
What is your adaptation process? How do you decide what to keep and what to remove, and find the visual storytelling equivalents from some of the most challenging source material (e.g. Silence). \
\
